{"name":"Windsurfer","hex":"#d7e2de","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"windsurfer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who windsurfs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windsurfer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Windsurfing","blocks":[{"text":"Windsurfing is a wind-propelled water sport that is a combination of sailing and surfing. It is also referred to as \"sailboarding\" and \"boardsailing\", and emerged in the late 1960s from the Californian aerospace and surf culture. Windsurfing gained a popular following across Europe and North America by the late 1970s and had achieved significant global popularity by the 1980s. Windsurfing became an Olympic sport in 1984."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Hood_river_windsurfers_20060701_0759.jpeg/330px-Hood_river_windsurfers_20060701_0759.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsurfing"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Darby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif/250px-Darby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Darby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Darby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif/250px-Darby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Darby sailboard, Popular Science, 1965","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADarby_sailboard%2C_Published_Popular_Science%2C_August_1965.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Windsurfpatent.jpg/500px-Windsurf